server: let a caller name the slot on the anthropic endpoint

Problem
-------
/v1/messages converts an anthropic body to the OAI shape through a whitelist:

    for (const auto & key : {"temperature", "top_p", "top_k", "stream",
                             "chat_template_kwargs"})

Anything not on the list is dropped, including id_slot. A router in front of
this server can then only guess which slot took a prompt, by reading id_slot
back out of the reply. That does not work either: to_json_anthropic never
emits __verbose.

Guessing from a poll is wrong most of the time, because the poll is seconds
old and reading a long prompt runs for minutes.

Fix
---
Add id_slot to the pass-through list, so a caller can say which slot should
serve the request. It is honoured by get_available_slot the same way it is on
the OAI endpoints.

diff --git a/tools/server/server-chat.cpp b/tools/server/server-chat.cpp
index a6fe3c6ba..a6674f66c 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-chat.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-chat.cpp
@@ -576,7 +576,11 @@ json server_chat_convert_anthropic_to_oai(const json & body) {
     }
 
     // Pass through common params
-    for (const auto & key : {"temperature", "top_p", "top_k", "stream", "chat_template_kwargs"}) {
+    // id_slot lets a caller say which slot should serve the request. Without
+    // it a router in front of this server can only guess which slot took a
+    // prompt, and guessing from a poll is wrong as often as not.
+    for (const auto & key : {"temperature", "top_p", "top_k", "stream", "chat_template_kwargs",
+                             "id_slot"}) {
         if (body.contains(key)) {
             oai_body[key] = body.at(key);
         }
